  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "2v1 with a pass in from the middle – everyone switches roles",
  "description": "A 2v1 game against one goal with a goalkeeper, in groups of three. The back (D) and one forward (A) start centrally in front of goal. The other forward (B) starts with the ball at the centre line. B plays the ball in to A and joins the attack straight away, and the two forwards try to create a chance against the lone back.\n\nAs soon as the ball is out of play everyone switches: the back steps up as the forward in front of goal, B who started from the centre becomes the new back, and A goes out to the centre line, takes a new ball and starts the next attack straight away. That way everyone plays every role. With more players: have the next group wait at the centre line and change groups after a few attacks.\n\nThe role changes keep the drill unpredictable, and the goalkeeper keeps facing new situations. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Make yourself available – show for the pass in and get free of the back."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Talk to each other: who has the ball, who goes to goal?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The player on the ball takes on the back so they have to choose."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Switch straight away when the ball is out of play – the next attack starts at once."
    }
  ],
